Grant BPF filesystem privileges for the Android 13 (fydroid) container.

The ARC++ (Android 13) container mounts its own bpffs at /sys/fs/bpf from
inside its user + mount namespace; Android 13 netd hard-requires a writable
/sys/fs/bpf for the in-container bpfloader. This 6.1 vendor tree is
Android-common-based and predates mainline v6.8, which made bpffs
userns-mountable (FS_USERNS_MOUNT) gated by an init-ns capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN)
check in bpf_fill_super. Without FS_USERNS_MOUNT the VFS rejects the
container's mount outright:

  libminijail[1]: cannot mount 'bpf' as '.../sys/fs/bpf' ...: Operation not
                  permitted

This backports both pieces at once and, like the fydroid 6.12 patch, relaxes
the gate from init-ns capable() to ns_capable(fc->user_ns, CAP_SYS_ADMIN) so
the container (which holds CAP_SYS_ADMIN only in its own userns) can mount
bpffs. In init_user_ns this is identical to upstream behaviour. Inert on
boards that do not run the Android container.

Mirror of chromeos-kernel-6_12 069-grant-bpf-privileges-for-android13.patch
(6.12 already carries FS_USERNS_MOUNT + the init-ns gate upstream, so that
version only flips capable() -> ns_capable(); 6.1 needs the full backport and
has no kernel/bpf/token.c). RE-CHECK ON KERNEL UPREV.

Index: kernel-6_1/kernel/bpf/inode.c
===================================================================
--- kernel-6_1.orig/kernel/bpf/inode.c
+++ kernel-6_1/kernel/bpf/inode.c
@@ -747,6 +747,21 @@ static int bpf_fill_super(struct super_block *sb, struct fs_context *fc)
 	struct inode *inode;
 	int ret;

+	/*
+	 * Mounting an instance of BPF FS requires privileges over the user
+	 * namespace that will own the superblock. Mainline gained this gate
+	 * together with FS_USERNS_MOUNT in v6.8; this 6.1 vendor tree predates
+	 * both. fydroid uses ns_capable() (rather than upstream's init-ns
+	 * capable()) so the ARC++ (Android 13) container can mount its own
+	 * bpffs from inside its user namespace -- Android 13 netd hard-requires
+	 * a writable /sys/fs/bpf for the in-container bpfloader. RE-CHECK ON
+	 * KERNEL UPREV (6.12 carries this upstream; see project-openfyde-patches
+	 * chromeos-kernel-6_12 069-grant-bpf-privileges-for-android13.patch).
+	 */
+	if (fc->user_ns != &init_user_ns &&
+	    !ns_capable(fc->user_ns, CAP_SYS_ADMIN))
+		return -EPERM;
+
 	ret = simple_fill_super(sb, BPF_FS_MAGIC, bpf_rfiles);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -801,6 +816,7 @@ static struct file_system_type bpf_fs_type = {
 	.init_fs_context = bpf_init_fs_context,
 	.parameters	= bpf_fs_parameters,
 	.kill_sb	= kill_litter_super,
+	.fs_flags	= FS_USERNS_MOUNT,
 };

 static int __init bpf_init(void)
